\section{Data Structures}

\subsection{Input State}

Three bytes representing the three input ports.  All bits are active-low:
0xFF means no buttons pressed.  When a key is held, the corresponding bit
is cleared to 0.

\begin{itemize}
\item \textbf{port\_48} (P1 joystick + fire): bits 0--3 = directions, bit 4 = fire
\item \textbf{port\_49} (system): bit 0 = 1P start, bit 1 = 2P start, bit 7 = coin
\item \textbf{port\_4a} (P2 joystick + fire): same layout as P1
\end{itemize}

<<input state struct>>=
struct InputState {
    uint8_t port_48 = 0xFF;  // P1: L=0, R=1, U=2, D=3, Fire=4
    uint8_t port_49 = 0xFF;  // System: 1P=0, 2P=1, Coin1=7
    uint8_t port_4a = 0xFF;  // P2: same layout as P1
};
@

